# _identity.env — UPSTREAM-IDENTITY drift oracle for the GENERATOR archetype.
#
# EXEMPLAR MEMBER = hugmesh-generator itself (this repo IS the base). These
# are the ORIGINAL literal token values the archetype recipe anchors carry in
# the READ-ONLY upstream base. NOT secrets, NOT tenant brand — upstream identity.
#
# scripts/validate-repo-templates.sh renders each recipe anchor's find AND replace
# with EXACTLY these values and asserts, per anchor:
#   (1) find@upstream still occurs in the freshly-pulled base  (anchor still bites)
#   (2) replace@upstream == find@upstream                      (round-trip no-op)
#
# renames[] is NOT part of the round-trip oracle (a rename is never a no-op —
# docs/BRANDING-hugmesh-systems.md != docs/BRANDING.md even at upstream
# values); the rename source's continued existence is what required:true
# enforces at render time, and the hermetic archetype test pins the behavior.
#
# Shell-sourced KEY=VALUE (same idiom as brands/*.conf).
BRAND_TITLE="HugMesh"
GENERATOR_ORG_GROUP="HugMesh/hugmesh-generator"
# ORG "HugMesh" under the single slug rule (lowercase, non-alnum -> '-').
ORG_SLUG="hugmesh-systems"
